# Columbus AI environment files
#
# Copy the template for your target environment (all three have the same keys):
#
#   Local Docker dev:  cp .env.local.example .env.local
#   Staging VPS:       cp .env.staging.example .env.staging
#   Production VPS:    cp .env.production.example .env.production
#
# Docker Compose (from repo root):
#   make up-dev          # uses .env.local + compose.dev.yml
#   make up-staging      # uses .env.staging + compose.staging.yml
#   make up-prod         # uses .env.production + compose.prod.yml
#
# Regenerate templates after editing env/profiles.ts:  pnpm env:sync-examples
# Verify key parity:                                   pnpm env:check
#
# See docs/env.md
